_handoff/rw-v2/legs/v12-attempt1-REJECTED.mdx:173:A known source can deliver a harmful artifact. Permitted work can still be wrong. A run using a skill does not establish that the skill caused the result. Fixed dependencies do not make probabilistic reasoning deterministic. The next question is whether the request, evidence, and authority survive long enough to judge the outcome. A <Term id="feature-contract">Feature Contract</Term> is one way to make those obligations explicit; [The Contract Is the Work](/essays/the-contract-is-the-work/) takes up that boundary.
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/v12-attempt1-REJECTED.mdx:204:      detail: 'SkillMeat manages artifact registration and deployment in my lab; that is one coordination implementation, not a requirement that every enterprise use one router.'
_handoff/rw-v2/legs/v12-attempt1-REJECTED.mdx:246:I place this work within the emerging discipline of <Term id="agentic-systems-engineering">**Agentic Systems Engineering**</Term>, already named in academic work by Sun and colleagues and in enterprise work by OutSystems.[^ase] This series examines my particular architecture through the systems I build and the failures they expose. Agentic SDLC is its application to software delivery. This reading path connects the questions; it isn't a one-to-one map of architecture layers.
